Hi David,
 
Thank you for contacting Plesk Technical Support.
 
At this time, Plesk does not yet support running applications on custom ports. Additionally, if opening port 8000, the application will be accessed directly and therefore cannot be secured with Plesk since requests would not be served by nginx. Securing it with a certificate would then be an administrative task to be performed on your end.
 
Instead, you should add the domain api.davidjgrimsley.com to Plesk and apply the following steps from this article:
Log into Plesk
Uncheck PHP Support option at Domain > api.davidjgrimsley.com > Dashboard > PHP
Uncheck Proxy mode option at Domain > api.davidjgrimsley.com > Hosting & DNS > Apache and Nginx Settings
mceclip1.png
Add the following to Domains > example.com > Apache & Nginx Settings > Additional nginx directives


        
        
location / {
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr;
proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
}
Click Apply 
 
Following this, you application should be available on api.davidjgrimsley.com on port 443 (standard HTTPS) and you may secure the domain like you would any other domain.
 
Let me know should you have any further questions.
Best regards,

