Hello David,
 
To make it an explanatory web page, you should either:
use the following configuration to ensure index.html is fetched locally (no need to re-enable PHP support):

        
        
location / { 
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr; 
proxy_set_header Host $http_host; 
proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000; 
}
    
# Serve /index.html directly 
location = /index.html { 
root /var/www/vhosts/davidjgrimsley.com/quantum-api.davidjgrimsley.com; 
}
 
set the location of the application to some other path (such as /api for example). In that case, you would not need to disable PHP support or Proxy Mode, as those are only disabled to avoid conflicts with the root location. You can then place an HTML or PHP page in the root to be displayed on access. This could also be applied to put the API on davidjgrimsley.com/api instead if desired
 
Let me know should you have any further questions.
 
 
