Hello David,
 
When checking in the server, I found that the 502 error occurs because your application, despite being correctly listening on port 8000, is not responding to requests:

        
        
root@romantic-gauss:~# ss -tlpn | grep 8000
LISTEN 0      2048                        0.0.0.0:8000       0.0.0.0:*    users:(("gunicorn",pid=2191541,fd=6),("gunicorn",pid=2191540,fd=6),("gunicorn",pid=2191344,fd=6),("gunicorn",pid=2191343,fd=6),("gunicorn",pid=2169935,fd=6))         
root@romantic-gauss:~# curl http://127.0.0.1:8000
curl: (56) Recv failure: Connection reset by peer
 
As a result, nginx returns a 502 error indicating that the application it is trying to communicate with does not work.
 
To correct this you should contact the application developer to troubleshoot it, as this is an issue that should be treated on their end.
 
As for the error:

        
        
Invalid nginx configuration: nginx: [emerg] duplicate location "/" in /var/www/vhosts/system/quantum-api.davidjgrimsley.com/conf/vhost_nginx.conf:5 nginx: configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test failedUnable to use the current nginx configuration file and to rollback to the previous version of the file because they both contain invalid configuration.
 
This occurs because PHP Support and/or Proxy Mode are enabled on the domain. You should either disable these before adding the directives, or modify the directives to use a different location than the root path.
